about the coronavirus pandemic. You know, I&nbsp;
got a few emails from people saying, David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.800
if you want to be fair, you've got to call out&nbsp;
Joe Biden for something that he recently said.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.880
Joe Biden recently said the pandemic is over.&nbsp;
That's not true. And if you're going to be fair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.360
you can't let that slide while I call out&nbsp;
anybody who says things that aren't true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.000
And Joe Biden did on 60 Minutes say the&nbsp;
pandemic is over and the pandemic is not over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.640
And I will make that case in a moment, but maybe&nbsp;
maybe not in the way you would assume I would make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.400
it. So let's first listen to what Joe Biden said.
Speaker 2: Mr. President, first Detroit Auto Show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:48.320
in three years. Yeah. Is the pandemic over? The&nbsp;
pandemic is over. We still have a problem with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.920
COVID. We're still doing a lot of work on it.&nbsp;
It's but the pandemic is over. If you notice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.880
no one's wearing masks. Everybody seems to be in&nbsp;
pretty good shape. And so I think it's changing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.680
And I think this is a perfect example of it.
Speaker 1: This is pretty silly. It really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.640
is. Now, there's two interpretations here. When&nbsp;
Joe Biden says, listen, the pandemic is over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:16.160
as evidenced by the auto show is back. There is&nbsp;
no masks and everyone here seems to be doing okay.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.040
You know, forget about the millions that that have&nbsp;
died for a second. But this really isn't true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:27.920
Now, this isn't about me. I am not saying I need&nbsp;
to hold on to every guideline we ever had. No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:33.440
I mean, I'm not wearing masks. I'm out in the&nbsp;
world. I'm doing things. This is not a question of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:40.720
of me. My behavior is basically back to normal.&nbsp;
But it's not true that the pandemic is over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.560
When you look at the sort of numbers that we&nbsp;
have right now in the United States, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.960
an average of somewhere between 60 and 90,000&nbsp;
new cases a day. When we had 100 cases a day at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:58.000
the start of the pandemic, it was a disaster. We&nbsp;
now have 60 to 90000 that we know of and probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.760
two or three times more from people doing&nbsp;
home tests are not getting tested at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.080
When you look at the death numbers,&nbsp;
we still have somewhere between,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:16.160
you know, three and 500 people dying every single&nbsp;
day from COVID. So here are the things Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:22.640
could have said that would have been true. We've&nbsp;
gotten accustomed to the current level of death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:29.200
from COVID, and we consider it normal and&nbsp;
acceptable and a fair exchange to going back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.160
